Cluster marker-gene reads into similarity-threshold OTUs and assemble
them into a \code{\link[phyloseq:phyloseq-class]{phyloseq::phyloseq-class()}} object with an \code{otu_table} of
per-sample abundances and the representative (seed/centroid) sequence of
each OTU in the \code{refseq} slot: reads are dereplicated per sample with
\href{https://github.com/torognes/vsearch}{vsearch}, pooled, dereplicated
again, and clustered with vsearch (\code{--cluster_size}, default) or
\href{https://github.com/torognes/swarm}{SWARM} (\code{d > 1} recommended).

This complements \code{\link[=asv2otu]{asv2otu()}}, which post-clusters ASVs already stored in
a phyloseq object: \code{cluster_reads()} starts one step earlier, directly
from sequence files or a vector of DNA sequences. Use \code{\link[=denoised_reads]{denoised_reads()}}
instead of this function to denoise reads into ASVs/zOTUs (dada2
pipeline, SWARM \code{d = 1} or vsearch UNOISE).
